 profile (the 30 m DSM includes tree canopy).","Road bumps and ruts in the drive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the road are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 40 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","The stupa is the Atlas maquette (a procedural model, not a survey). Published (Wikipedia): a square plinth about 4 m thick (read here as its height) and a hemispherical dome 7 m high and 21 m across. The 34 m square plinth width is NOT in that source: the maquette note cites a heritage source for it, which was not checked here, so it is unverified. The drum, the stair on the east side and the plinth profile are estimated.","The ground is levelled to a 30 m terrace round the stupa so the plinth sits flat; the surrounding slope is the real DEM.","The walk from the road to the stupa has no mapped footpath: it is the easiest route over the DEM.","Rubble and wall stubs around the plinth are drawn after Commons photos; their positions are illustrative.","The walk from the end of the road follows the mapped OSM footpath for 0.0 km; the last 0.18 km is not mapped and is traced over the ground (easiest slope on the DEM).","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"Amluk-Dara Stupa maquette (Tiny Atlas, procedural)","use":"the stupa's plinth, drum and dome; the 21 m diameter and the 4 m plinth follow the published figures (Wikipedia); the 34 m plinth width is unverified and the other proportions are estimated","licence":"Tiny Atlas own procedural geometry (backend/tools/blender/stupa.py)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amluk-Dara_stupa"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the village road (unclassified, 4.5 km) that passes 170 m east of the stupa, and the stupa point (tourism=attraction)","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}